      "claim_id": "c2",
      "status": "supported",
      "witness": null,
      "reason": "The claim correctly identifies EXT_SOURCE_2 as the strongest driver of risk: its attribution (+0.8147) has the largest absolute contribution among all attributions. It correctly states that this factor increases risk (matching direction: 'increases_risk') and references the model's reference background (TreeSHAP expected value). The value 0.157 is the observed fact, not the attribution — but the claim does not misrepresent the attribution as the value; it correctly links the score to its effect. No rule is broken."
